      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did change the location of codegen to `src/gfxstream/codegen/`, so one can just do `git format-patch HEAD~{n}` to generate patches that can be easily applied to the Mesa copy.\n\nAs for history preservation, we\u0027ve used non-history preserving methods in the past (aosp/2824967) and it really didn\u0027t make much difference.\n\nIf we want to move the `src/gfxstream/codegen`, one would have to do `git log --follow src/gfxstream/codegen/xml/vk_gfxstream.xml`, but that\u0027s not too different from `git log -- codegen/vulkan/vulkan-docs-next/xml/vk_gfxstream.xml` (`git blame` would not be preserved across directory moves).  Plus, the Mesa move itself used a history preserving method, though here it would result in 90 commits.\n\nIf we really need to find something in the history, between Gerrit, branches, and the repositories own history -- the means do exist.  So \"meh\" on the history preservation.",
